                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_94">Cambridge,
                        Cambridgeshire. Franciscan convent</orgName><p>'Iste liber constat fratri
                        Thome Trumpyton ordinis minorum sacre theologie professoris, precium viij
                        marc' (fol. 1v).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Has cauciones (Cambridge) of Hugh Damlett
                     (afterwards master of Pembroke and rector of St Peter-upon-Cornhill, London)
                     dated 1435 and 1438, and of John Clynt (cf. Peterhouse MSS 77, 255, 263 and
                     Gonville and Caius MS 510) dated 1441. Later belonged to Thomas Trumpyngton
                     STP, OFM (who in 1465 was chaplain of the house of Poor Clares at Denny, Cambs,
                     and owned BL MS Cotton Cleopatra C.ix fols. 63--165 and perhaps Vatican MS
                     Ottobon. lat. 352).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Given to Balliol by William Gray, bishop of
                     Ely (d. 1478).</provenance>
